[{"finding":"When a value crosses a process/language boundary to multiple consumers, fix moves to the consumers, never to the emitter — the emitter's spelling is treated as fixed even when it predates the consumers","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/observations/run-audit.ts:40"],"released":false},{"finding":"A cross-boundary consistency test derives its expected value by parsing the authoritative source's own literal, rather than trusting a second constant hand-copied beside it","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/capture/dispatch-action.test.ts:29"],"released":false},{"finding":"When historical records violate a newly-introduced invariant and cannot be repaired, the entries that violate it are dropped with a logged count, and the pipeline proceeds on the resulting wider approximation rather than failing the run","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/observations/run-audit.ts:130"],"released":false},{"finding":"A trigger gate is chosen from the event field that identifies who performed the act (sender/author_association) rather than a label or state that anyone can cause to exist.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/shape.yml:44"],"released":false},{"finding":"When repairing a stale citation, the session sometimes resolved the surrounding claim's substance (introducing a new \"decided\" state, e.g. branch protection declined) rather than only replacing the dead pointer, without flagging that as a separate judgement call.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/gauntlet-hook.mjs:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"When removing a locally-mirrored artifact whose canonical copy lives at an external URL, delete the local citation path entirely rather than keeping it alongside the URL","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["GOAL.md:227"],"released":false},{"finding":"Test doubles for two dependencies whose relative order matters are logged into one shared call-sequence array rather than separate counters, so ordering assertions read off a single list.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/back-stamp.test.ts:233"],"released":false},{"finding":"Assertions over a corpus that can grow over time are expressed as properties (plus their logical converse) instead of a pinned literal count, so the test doesn't go red merely because the corpus grew.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/missing-trailer.test.ts:96"],"released":false},{"finding":"A non-gate helper degrades by skipping work it can't complete rather than failing outright, reserving fail-closed behavior for the actual gate that will catch the same problem downstream.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["bin/new-adr:101"],"released":false},{"finding":"A file meant partly for model injection separates human-facing explanatory prose from the injected content behind a delimiter, and the accessor throws rather than silently returning an empty or over-inclusive result if the split fails","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/to-tickets.ts:286"],"released":false},{"finding":"A small error-preserving-and-rethrow wrapper is duplicated at a second failure site instead of generalized into one shared helper, despite the new function's own comment describing it as making \"the same bargain\" as the existing one","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/to-tickets.ts:393"],"released":false},{"finding":"A test's fixture parser splits on a maximally permissive delimiter and asserts shape explicitly afterward, rather than matching a pattern that could silently skip a malformed entry","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/vocabulary.test.ts:21"],"released":false},{"finding":"Validate every item in a batch before performing any side effect on any of them, so a single invalid item leaves zero effects rather than a partial write.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:138"],"released":false},{"finding":"When two options represent mutually exclusive semantics, refuse the call at the very top of the function before any other work runs, rather than picking a resolution order between them.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stage.ts:285"],"released":false},{"finding":"A gate that can silently drop a true positive must be built from deterministic lookups against already-produced artifacts rather than a model's judgement, because a wrong drop is invisible downstream.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/structural-refusal.ts:80"],"released":false},{"finding":"A `gh`-workflow-YAML test reads and parses the workflow file directly (`readFileSync` + `yaml.parse`) instead of using the shared `readWorkflow` helper this diff introduces for exactly that purpose, unlike every sibling workflow test in the same diff.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/review.test.ts:296"],"released":false},{"finding":"Parsing the issue number back out of `gh issue create`'s stdout (a `/\\/issues\\/(\\d+)\\s*$/`-style regex plus a \"could not parse an issue number\" throw) is reimplemented verbatim per module instead of being factored into one shared helper.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/publish-findings.ts:16"],"released":false},{"finding":"Cross-lane dispatch event-type constants get exactly one declaration, and are guarded by a test that reads the wire name out of every receiving workflow's `if:` and checks it against that single constant, rather than each side testing its own imported copy.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/immutable-set.test.ts:135"],"released":false},{"finding":"A `repository_dispatch` trigger branch carries no separate sender/actor authorization check (no `sender.login` or `author_association` gate), because sending the dispatch itself already required write access, so the send is treated as the authorization.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/spec-workflow.test.ts:75"],"released":false},{"finding":"A dispatch payload field's encoding (comma-joined string vs. repeated `key[]=` array) is chosen based on how the specific downstream job parses it — comma-joined for a shell string-compare job, a real repeated array for a job that reads it as JSON.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/implement.ts:300"],"released":false},{"finding":"An issue's label is applied on the same `gh issue create` call that files it, never as a follow-up `issue edit`, so the issue is never observable in an unlabeled state that other automation could read as an ordinary issue.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/publish.ts:139"],"released":false},{"finding":"A cross-call ordering guarantee is tested by comparing call indices (`findIndex`/`toBeGreaterThan`) to prove one action happened strictly after another, rather than asserting only that both calls occurred.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shape/accept.test.ts:291"],"released":false},{"finding":"An exemption from an automated reachability/dead-code gate must carry an inline prose reason at the exemption site itself, never a silent name in an ignore list","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:57",".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:93","knip.config.ts:79"],"released":true},{"finding":"A baseline that grandfathers existing debt into a new gate must only ratchet down and gate solely on new additions, never re-grow or serve as a permanent allowlist","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/wiring-baseline.json:3","docs/agents/clone-gate.md:46"],"released":true},{"finding":"A check-command allowlist keyed to specific remote-reading commands (gh api/issue/pr/run, curl, wget), not a broader \"reaches outside the repository\" heuristic, because a deliberately-outside-repo but locally-readable path must still pass","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.ts:33"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a test double must echo back untrusted string content that may contain shell metacharacters, write it to a file the stub reads back rather than interpolating it into the stub script's own source","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.test.ts:76"],"released":false},{"finding":"Context a model needs for correctness is inlined directly into its prompt rather than granted through a tool or allow-list, so its reach is a fact about what was built rather than an instruction it must choose to honor.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:95"],"released":false},{"finding":"Content rendered into a prompt for a model is left uncapped rather than truncated, since a partial view recreates the same guessing problem the full view was added to remove.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:101"],"released":false},{"finding":"Structurally distinct absent-states (a claimed file not yet created vs. a ticket that claims no files at all) are given separate, explicit sentinel messages rather than collapsed into one empty or undefined representation.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:80"],"released":false},{"finding":"A body-section parser is relocated to the shared module that owns the data shape it reads, once a second caller needs the same reading, rather than staying in the file of whichever caller wrote it first.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/ticket-shape.ts:176"],"released":false},{"finding":"A structural text matcher built to read a config/workflow file strips comments before matching, because prose explaining a decision can itself contain text indistinguishable from a real match.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["tests/acceptance/workflow-shape.fixture.ts:94"],"released":false},{"finding":"A counter that recomputes its entire result set from scratch every run is entitled to close its own standing issue when the count reaches zero, but a counter that only sees a partial slice of state per run must not, since it lacks the full picture to justify closing.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:341"],"released":false},{"finding":"A failure in a side-effecting close/retire call is caught, logged, and dropped rather than surfaced as a run failure, because the operation is idempotent and the next scheduled run will naturally retry it.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:354"],"released":false},{"finding":"When an action posts a record that justifies a subsequent state-changing call to an external system, the record-writing call must be ordered before the state-changing call, so a downstream reader of history never observes the change without its justification already present.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:351"],"released":false},{"finding":"A CI checkout must use fetch-depth: 0 whenever the job runs a test suite that may assert facts about git history rather than the working tree, since shallow clones make history-dependent checks fail on venue artefacts rather than real facts","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:112"],"released":false},{"finding":"Machine-written trailers/markers must be stripped from content before it's shown to a model and deterministically re-appended after the model's output is written back, rather than trusting the model to preserve them verbatim","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/publish.ts:131"],"released":false},{"finding":"A scripted test fake with an ordered list of per-call responses should throw once it runs out of responses rather than silently repeating the last one","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stage.fake.ts:37"],"released":false},{"finding":"When new work must happen between a decision and its effects, split a combined decide-and-apply function into a pure counting/deciding half and a single shared applying half, rather than duplicating the apply logic per caller","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A stage that revises output already validated by an earlier decision should not have that decision re-checked against its output, since there is no remaining channel to resolve a fresh objection","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:416"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a stage's structured output is naturally a single scalar value, wrap it with a scalar-rooted output schema instead of modeling it as a synthetic single-field object type","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/reconcile.ts:56"],"released":false},{"finding":"An ADR superseded by a later one gets a \"Status: superseded by ADR-NNNN\" line added near its top.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["docs/adr/0039-the-governor-does-not-ship-concurrency-is-bounded-by-ready-d.md:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"A wait loop that polls an external verdict bounds itself by a fixed attempt count rather than elapsed wall-clock time, so a test can drive it by counting reads instead of advancing a clock.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:208"],"released":false},{"finding":"Subprocess-spawning logic reused by more than one lane is extracted into shared/ rather than one lane importing another lane's module at runtime.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/close-ticket.ts:13"],"released":false},{"finding":"A reader's dependency on a specific field existing in an API response is proven against a payload recorded from the live API, not only against a hand-written fake.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/closing-prs.fixtures/issue-237-closed-by.json:1"],"released":false},{"finding":"Exit code 2 from a check is read as \"could not run\" only for checks that explicitly opt into that convention, never applied globally, since third-party tools can use exit 2 for a genuine finding.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["bin/gauntlet:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A repair step outside a run's primary claim (e.g. regenerating a derived artifact) never fails the run when it errors; the failure is logged and left for a downstream gate to catch by name.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/regenerate-artifacts.ts:72"],"released":false},{"finding":"Fake test IDs for two related-but-distinct entities (e.g. an issue and its closing PR) are deliberately given different numbering schemes so a reader that confuses the two fails the test rather than passing by coincidence.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.test.ts:54"],"released":false},{"finding":"A caught exception is treated as the specific case it's meant to handle only after positively confirming that case via authoritative post-failure state, and re-thrown unchanged when that confirmation fails","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:387"],"released":false},{"finding":"State that a subsequent cleanup or abort operation will destroy is read out before that operation runs","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:391"],"released":false},{"finding":"An expensive or irreversible operation's precondition is checked and the call skipped with an explicit no-op message when the precondition doesn't hold, rather than invoking it speculatively","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A non-merge outcome only reddens the automation run when the outcome reflects a problem with the diff under test, not merely because nothing was merged","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:622"],"released":false},{"finding":"When one file's output format is parsed by another, a test reads both files' sources and asserts the parser's pattern matches the exact string the producer emits, so a rewording in either fails a test instead of breaking silently at runtime","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:278"],"released":false},{"finding":"A status/label constant with meaning shared across independently-triggered lanes is defined once and imported, never re-declared as a duplicate string literal","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"Cheap regex prefilter selects candidate lines before a precise structured parse decides the actual verdict, preserving both performance and correctness","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/_hook.py:399"],"released":false},{"finding":"A hook's per-subprocess deadlines are treated as a shared wall-clock budget that must stay under the harness's registered timeout, with a test asserting the sum against that registered value rather than just documenting it","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/close-gate.py:79"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a signal is unknowable, the code defaults to whichever answer is safe for that specific gate's failure direction, not a universal fail-open/fail-closed default","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/_hook.py:453"],"released":false},{"finding":"A concurrency group's key must scope to the specific subject a run acts on (e.g. per-PRD, per-issue), never a fixed/shared key, so unrelated subjects don't serialize behind each other","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/to-tickets.yml:63"],"released":false},{"finding":"A \"Cite, don't restate\" trim names a plain code comment (not a helper docstring or an ADR) as the rationale's home","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:116",".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:210",".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:264"],"released":true},{"finding":"Escalation to the owner goes on the ticket (issue), never the pull request, so the tracker is the single place an agent checks for stalled work","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/needs-human.ts:29"],"released":false},{"finding":"A stopped/failed lane always pairs a machine-readable label with a human-readable comment explaining what was tried — never one without the other","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:171"],"released":false},{"finding":"A push/commit made by a lane that may run after another lane already rewrote the branch's history uses `--force-with-lease`, never a plain `push`","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:157"],"released":false},{"finding":"A lane that repairs or rebuilds a branch re-checks out and rebases onto trunk immediately before doing lane-specific work, so the code that runs is trunk's rather than whatever the branch originally forked from","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/fixer.yml:249"],"released":false},{"finding":"A dispatch/event handler reads state (e.g. ticket/PR status) before spending any model or expensive work, and refuses cheaply rather than let the expensive stage discover staleness after the fact","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/implement.ts:598"],"released":false},{"finding":"Idempotency/attempt-tracking for an unattended retry loop is derived from durable, externally-inspectable state (commit messages, marker comments) rather than an in-memory or file-based counter, so the count survives the process that made it ending","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:277"],"released":false},{"finding":"When polling GitHub Actions state that may belong to a run still in progress, address reads by job id rather than run id, since `gh run view <run> --log` refuses to return anything while any job in the run is unfinished, but `gh run view --job <id> --log` only blocks on that specific job.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:284"],"released":false},{"finding":"Test fixture defaults should be derived from a more fundamental related field instead of requiring both to be stated independently, so a fixture describing one fact (e.g. a job mid-flight) can't drift out of sync with a redundant restatement of the same fact (e.g. the run's own status).","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.test.ts:157"],"released":false},{"finding":"Repeated inline fixture literals that represent the same semantic verdict should be extracted into named constants describing that verdict, rather than duplicated ad hoc at each call site.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.test.ts:58"],"released":false},{"finding":"A fuzzy \"same clone, re-cut\" match is recognized by combining same-file-pair identity, token-signature containment (not exact equality), and a size-growth cap below the minimum reportable clone size — a deliberately loose-but-fenced equality rule rather than exact matching.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:279"],"released":false},{"finding":"When multiple stale baseline entries and multiple newly-found clones could plausibly pair up, the ambiguity is resolved by a fixed deterministic ordering (stale entries sorted by hash, smallest candidate wins) rather than leaving the match order unspecified.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:299"],"released":false},{"finding":"A baseline entry whose stored fragment fails to re-hash to its own recorded hash is treated as a gate failure (exit code reserved for \"could not run\") rather than as an ordinary finding, distinguishing data-integrity corruption from legitimate content drift.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:337"],"released":false},{"finding":"Recorded line-number metadata on a baseline entry is deliberately left stale rather than refreshed on every write, trading display accuracy for diff stability against unrelated line-shifting edits.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:542"],"released":false},{"finding":"A one-time schema migration (backfilling a new optional field onto existing records) is folded into the routine maintenance operation rather than implemented as a separate one-off migration step.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:672"],"released":false},{"finding":"Match \"already recorded\" evidence against a value's canonical serialized form (its URL), never against loose numbers or dates parsed out of free-form prose, since a human comment coincidentally containing a matching number would be misread as evidence.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/dead-lanes.ts:172"],"released":false},{"finding":"Scope a fetch to only the bounded set of items about to be used, rather than the single bulk/listing call that would return everything, even when the bulk call would be simpler to write.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/run-watchdog.ts:203"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a read of a bounded window is known to be incomplete, skip any conclusion that depends on having seen the whole window rather than drawing it from partial data.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/run-watchdog.ts:253"],"released":false},{"finding":"Treat absence of negative evidence as insufficient to declare recovery/success; require an explicit positive event as proof before reversing a standing state.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/run-watchdog.ts:308"],"released":false},{"finding":"A failed write in an idempotent, recomputing process is logged and dropped rather than thrown, trusting the next scheduled run to retry it.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/run-watchdog.ts:318"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a signal is rung from inside the very run it names, the receiver must poll until that run reaches a terminal state before reading its output, and fail loudly (non-zero exit) rather than silently succeeding if the wait times out.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/fixer.yml:164"],"released":false},{"finding":"An idempotency marker for a dedup check must be written as the first effectful step, before any costly or state-changing work, so a crash mid-run still leaves a later retry a no-op.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/fixer.yml:242"],"released":false},{"finding":"When one underlying event can be signaled through multiple trigger doors, the concurrency group must be keyed on the underlying event's own id rather than the triggering event's id, so the doors queue behind each other instead of racing.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/fixer.yml:86"],"released":false},{"finding":"Elevated write permissions are scoped to a single dedicated job via a job-level permissions block, leaving sibling jobs that only judge/read on the workflow-level restricted default.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:330"],"released":false},{"finding":"A single job gated with always() plus explicit per-dependency result checks aggregates multiple upstream job outcomes to guarantee exactly-one downstream signal, rather than duplicating an if:failure() step in each upstream job.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:315"],"released":false},{"finding":"Use a `null` (not `undefined`) sentinel to represent an explicit override of a defaulted parameter, since passing `undefined` re-triggers the default","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:244"],"released":false},{"finding":"Prefer a closed allowlist of recognized file extensions over a loose \"looks like it has an extension\" heuristic when detecting file paths in prose, to avoid false positives on things like property access or abbreviations","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.ts:169"],"released":false},{"finding":"Detect a forbidden reference by matching raw source text rather than parsing an AST, accepting false positives as the cheaper failure mode over building a parser that must cover every possible access pattern","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/push-gate.ts:106"],"released":false},{"finding":"When two independent lanes need to perform the same kind of side-effecting write (e.g. filing the same category of issue), consolidate it into one shared function rather than letting each lane keep its own copy, so the two writes can't drift apart","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/spec-gap.ts:37"],"released":false},{"finding":"Pass through an in-memory value produced earlier in the same run instead of reading it back from where it was persisted, so the read and the write can never diverge","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:282"],"released":false},{"finding":"An action's effect is verified by reading the system's actual state afterward rather than trusted from the actor's self-reported account of what it did","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:176"],"released":false},{"finding":"An attempt that produces no observable change is excluded from a capped attempt count rather than recorded as a spent attempt","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:424"],"released":false},{"finding":"A parser handles only the input shapes known to occur in this repo and documents the acknowledged gap, rather than fully replicating the upstream tool's spec","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:190"],"released":false},{"finding":"A parsing grammar (the `CODING_STANDARDS.md` entry regexes) is duplicated between its source module and an ADR-0032-mandated acceptance-test copy, with no test asserting the two definitions stay identical — unlike every other duplicated constant in this same change, which pairs the duplicate with an \"agrees with\" test.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/ratify/standards.ts:18","tests/acceptance/296-ratifier-standards-are-well-formed.test.ts:44"],"released":true},{"finding":"A monotonic per-file counter used to key per-test isolated resources, incremented in a shared `beforeEach` rather than derived from vitest's own test identity","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/isolate-checkpoints.setup.ts:53"],"released":false},{"finding":"A setupFiles entry that eagerly creates a directory at import time (once per worker) while deferring the actual per-use resource creation to the consuming code's own mkdirSync, rather than creating it itself","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/isolate-checkpoints.setup.ts:49"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a signal needed for a decision cannot be determined, refuse/error rather than treating the unreadable state as equivalent to the empty/zero case","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["bin/close-ticket:342"],"released":false},{"finding":"A stub for an external CLI in tests answers every call with one fixed canned payload rather than routing responses by call sequence, since callers can inspect the call log directly for what happened","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stub-gh.fixture.ts:44"],"released":false},{"finding":"Drive a test through the real process boundary (actual binary spawned against a stub) instead of at function level specifically when the defect being guarded against is that something never reached across that boundary","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/